2. Biomni
   https://github.com/snap-stanford/Biomni, commit 400c1f366b96a35ca253e13c9b06c5076af41d65
   Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright the Biomni authors.
   The text of the license is in src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_package/LICENSE.
   Biomni has no NOTICE file of its own.

   Copied without modification (checked file by file against that commit):
     src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_package/biomni/   the tool functions, their descriptions,
                                                      the protocols and database schemas they
                                                      read, the know-how documents, and the
                                                      modules they import (175 files)
     src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_package/license_info.md
     src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_package/LICENSE
     src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_env/              the environment files the sandbox image
                                                      is built from (9 files)
     src/virtual_lab/biomni_env_desc.py               from biomni/env_desc.py, below its
                                                      docstring

   Adapted. These files of Lumi reproduce or follow parts of Biomni's code, prompts, or data
   tables. Each says in its header which parts, from where, and how it departs from Biomni:
     src/virtual_lab/benchmarks.py          the benchmarks' prompts, option shuffling, scoring
                                            rules, metrics, and output classes
     src/virtual_lab/resources.py           the resource retrieval prompt and its parser, and
                                            the listing of tools, data, and software
     src/virtual_lab/evaluation.py          the prompt that reads an answer out of a transcript
     src/virtual_lab/llm.py                 the choice of provider by model name
     src/virtual_lab/papers.py              the prompts that read a paper for tasks, databases,
                                            and software
     src/virtual_lab/paper_batch.py         reading many papers and counting what they share
     src/virtual_lab/function_generator.py  the prompt that writes a function for a task
     src/virtual_lab/sandbox/Dockerfile     installs Biomni's environment files in the order
                                            of Biomni's biomni_env/setup.sh

   Not included. The data lake (76 files, about 11 GB) is fetched from Biomni's release bucket
   when a person asks (download_data_lake, or the interface). Biomni's benchmark files are
   fetched from where Biomni fetches them, and are checked against pinned hashes.

   The data lake and the tools are made of other people's datasets and software, under their
   own licenses. Several permit non-commercial use only, and several need a license for
   commercial use. src/virtual_lab/sandbox/biomni_package/license_info.md, which is Biomni's,
   lists them. Check them before any commercial use.

   Huang, K., Zhang, S., Wang, H. et al. Biomni: A General-Purpose Biomedical AI Agent.
   bioRxiv (2025).

