4. Software Lumi installs and does not copy
   The Python and JavaScript packages Lumi depends on are installed from their registries,
   not copied into this repository, and are under their own licenses. Nearly all are
   permissive (MIT, BSD, ISC, Apache-2.0). The exceptions are used unmodified as libraries:
   certifi, orjson, and tqdm are MPL-2.0 (orjson and tqdm with MIT or Apache-2.0 code); pyphen,
   which WeasyPrint brings in for the optional pdf extra, is licensed under a choice of
   GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL-2.0-or-later, or MPL-1.1; and two packages used only while the pages
   are built, sharp-libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later) and caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0), are not part of
   what is served. The software in the sandbox image (samtools, BLAST, R and its packages,
   PLINK, and the rest of Biomni's environment) is installed when a person builds the image on
   their own machine, under its own licenses. The image is not distributed.

